{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20","id":1248244,"title":"How are you liking Wr20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-20T16:28:03-07:00","id":1248244,"title":"How are you liking Wr20?","content":"I liked Wr20. Did you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T04:19:27-07:00","id":1249092,"title":"","content":"I did. It's excellent. Very much the Revised Edition we deserved.<br /> <br /> One question for anyone who cares to answer: Willpower is still two freebies, unlike every other WoD game. Is this intentional, due to the higher starting Willpower, do you think (it was pointed out in the errata thread, which makes me think it was left in for a purpose)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T13:56:00-07:00","id":1249777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1249092#post1249092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did. It's excellent. Very much the Revised Edition we deserved.<br /> <br /> One question for anyone who cares to answer: Willpower is still two freebies, unlike every other WoD game. Is this intentional, due to the higher starting Willpower, do you think (it was pointed out in the errata thread, which makes me think it was left in for a purpose)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it that Willpower is especially important for Wraiths? If that's the case then I'd happily change it so that in M20 the cost is doubled. Willpower isn't *as* important to Vampires or Garou/Fera; it's a great resource and a way to resist mind-control, but for Mages Willpower is a cap to all Sphere levels (so if you have 5 and lose a point, you can't use level 5 spheres), a way to avoid paradox murdering you and a great way to get the successes you need for magick (where a single success is worth a lot).<br /> <br /> How important do you think Willpower is in Wr20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T13:47:25-07:00","id":1250528,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing something to be desired with this game ...<br /> <br /> Why in the world are so many level 5 Arcani no longer worth spending experience on, or not worth using the Pathos necessary to activate their effects.<br /> <br /> To have a Wraith who is formidable, with an imposing presence do to their high Levels they have achieved in their Arcani; you basically have to scrap this book, and use the old 1998 2cnd edition release.<br /> <br /> I guess in an age where the new generation needs to have their participation ribbons, that mentality has bled its way into the rpg world. Tone down the more powerful characteristics of the game mechanics in order to make everyone seem ... Equal ... even though this is supposed to be a Horror related game, where Equality is a luxury; because that means you haven't met the big bad bump in the night ... yet!<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T19:49:17-07:00","id":1251266,"title":"","content":"Its pretty damn awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T07:47:47-07:00","id":1251913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1249777#post1249777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it that Willpower is especially important for Wraiths? If that's the case then I'd happily change it so that in M20 the cost is doubled. Willpower isn't *as* important to Vampires or Garou/Fera; it's a great resource and a way to resist mind-control, but for Mages Willpower is a cap to all Sphere levels (so if you have 5 and lose a point, you can't use level 5 spheres), a way to avoid paradox murdering you and a great way to get the successes you need for magick (where a single success is worth a lot).<br /> <br /> How important do you think Willpower is in Wr20?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important for fending off the Shadow and the pull of Oblivion, but also, characters start at Willpower 5, whereas in Vampire they start off with 1-5 Willpower. That may be the reason why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1250528#post1250528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm seeing something to be desired with this game ...<br /> <br /> Why in the world are so many level 5 Arcani no longer worth spending experience on, or not worth using the Pathos necessary to activate their effects.<br /> <br /> To have a Wraith who is formidable, with an imposing presence do to their high Levels they have achieved in their Arcani; you basically have to scrap this book, and use the old 1998 2cnd edition release.<br /> <br /> I guess in an age where the new generation needs to have their participation ribbons, that mentality has bled its way into the rpg world. Tone down the more powerful characteristics of the game mechanics in order to make everyone seem ... Equal ... even though this is supposed to be a Horror related game, where Equality is a luxury; because that means you haven't met the big bad bump in the night ... yet!<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the powers seem nerfed. For instance, you could use cool thematic powers like Ride the Electron Highway at Inhabit 2, which felt appropriate given that Phantom Wings is Argos 2. But the new rules are generally more detailed, so you can just move the powers around if you need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T08:49:05-07:00","id":1251922,"title":"","content":"I doubt that level 5 powers have been weakened to appeal to &quot;SJWs&quot;. Maybe since wraith is a game more focused on personal horror they wanted to reduce the maximum power level of player characters? Regardless I've never seen a socially liberal person asking that powers be toned down so that high power characters and low power characters have closer power levels. I can understand being annoyed at Arcanoi getting weaker but this just feels like a huge leap in reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:37:23-07:00","id":1251936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1250528#post1250528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess in an age where the new generation needs to have their participation ribbons, that mentality has bled its way into the rpg world. Tone down the more powerful characteristics of the game mechanics in order to make everyone seem ... Equal ... even though this is supposed to be a Horror related game, where Equality is a luxury; because that means you haven't met the big bad bump in the night ... yet!<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... that is some grade A paranoid bullshit right there.<br /> <br /> 1) Participation trophies were a thing baby boomer parents did. It\u2019s not a thing millennials or Gen z wanted or are particularly noted as as giving their own kids.<br /> <br /> 2) Panning down certain level 5 powers is about making the different arcanoi more balanced with each other, not because anyone was complaining Arcanoi 5 characters in general are too powerful - but when certain Arcanoi grossly outclass others it creates \u201cone true builds\u201d which is boring.<br /> <br /> Now, you may think that isn\u2019t as fun design, which is fine, but that\u2019s the motivating reason behind it, not something involving thinly-veiled euphemisms for thinking racism and homophobia, etc, are bad things like those whiny brats today do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:16:54-07:00","id":1251971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1251936#post1251936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow... that is some grade A paranoid bullshit right there.<br /> <br /> 1) Participation trophies were a thing baby boomer parents did. It\u2019s not a thing millennials or Gen z wanted or are particularly noted as as giving their own kids.<br /> <br /> 2) Panning down certain level 5 powers is about making the different arcanoi more balanced with each other, not because anyone was complaining Arcanoi 5 characters in general are too powerful - but when certain Arcanoi grossly outclass others it creates \u201cone true builds\u201d which is boring.<br /> <br /> Now, you may think that isn\u2019t as fun design, which is fine, but that\u2019s the motivating reason behind it, not something involving thinly-veiled euphemisms for thinking racism and homophobia, etc, are bad things like those whiny brats today do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest participation trophies are memorials of southern civil war generals, pass it on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T19:13:32-07:00","id":1253188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1251936#post1251936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow... that is some grade A paranoid bullshit right there.<br /> <br /> 1) Participation trophies were a thing baby boomer parents did. It\u2019s not a thing millennials or Gen z wanted or are particularly noted as as giving their own kids.<br /> <br /> 2) Panning down certain level 5 powers is about making the different arcanoi more balanced with each other, not because anyone was complaining Arcanoi 5 characters in general are too powerful - but when certain Arcanoi grossly outclass others it creates \u201cone true builds\u201d which is boring.<br /> <br /> Now, you may think that isn\u2019t as fun design, which is fine, but that\u2019s the motivating reason behind it, not something involving thinly-veiled euphemisms for thinking racism and homophobia, etc, are bad things like those whiny brats today do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think anyone aware of the old 2cnd edition Level 5 Arcanoi could plainly see what the motivation behind it was.<br /> <br /> And, making the higher levels lesser in effect, and not scary abilities by the Ghosts you wouldn't want to cross, makes a perfect analogy for wanting them &quot;Balanced&quot; suggests someone who would rather watch a game played, where everyone is equal, and nobody is keeping score.<br /> <br /> Actually, Baby Boomers were the ones who not only drove cars without wearing Seat belts ... they were raised to purchase cars that didn't even have seat belts to begin with. They played Football where tackling head first was not only encouraged, it was expected. And Concussions were just part of the sport.<br /> <br /> The early 20th century Parents built the infrastructure we have, And left a growing industry for their children. The Baby Boomers were more blue collar than any in history, which became a middle class society. It was no longer the haves &amp; the have nots. There was now a have some populace ... They made a culture where their children would compete for jobs, teaching competition is the way to get ahead.<br /> <br /> What you are mistaking as the Baby Boomer generation, is the lull of hippy nonsense that happened in between. From the Free Lovers, to the early 80's, those were the ones who created this, everyone is special, unique and fair play is equality Garbley-gook.<br /> <br /> But, we GenXers did not do a whole lot to push back against it. Or, at least we didn't do enough to prevent it from getting to where it is today.<br /> <br /> The millennials have merely embraced it. Not all of them, but a great portion, to the point that GenX and the Mellennial perspectives clash regularly.<br /> <br /> However, that being typed ... gaming industries are a product of capitol achievement. Even those who wish they were as cutting edge as they would like to pretend to be. It is most definitely an industry which caters to a particular demographic. More &amp; more, that demographic is is the Mellennial generation ... understandably, because they still have Young Money. And the Generation that is being raised now, is a wild m\u00e9lange of children of parents from GenX who waited until their 40's to birth, and Millennial parents.<br /> <br /> The ideals of that generation is going to see major clashing of the wills with massive degrees in perspectives attempting to coalesce a single voice.<br /> <br /> And whats sad is, there happens to be a sick vocal force in today's media, who want to shame people for not allowing children to make adult decisions ... It sure isn't the Baby Boomers doing it.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T11:51:27-07:00","id":1253336,"title":"","content":"What in the name of Charon?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T17:04:18-07:00","id":1253421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1253188#post1253188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think anyone aware of the old 2cnd edition Level 5 Arcanoi could plainly see what the motivation behind it was.<br /> <br /> And, making the higher levels lesser in effect, and not scary abilities by the Ghosts you wouldn't want to cross, makes a perfect analogy for wanting them &quot;Balanced&quot; suggests someone who would rather watch a game played, where everyone is equal, and nobody is keeping score.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot speak to the rest of your points, I can't even speak to most of the above because to do that I'd have to be able to follow it. I'd suggest not assuming that everyone plainly sees whatever it is you plainly see. But I digress...<br /> <br /> I'm just going to respond to the single point (possibly one you weren't even making) that game balance is about appeasement. And I suppose it is, in the same sense that making a good movie is about giving the audience something they want to see. Which is to say that's not what appeasement is. Games live or die by balance, and the subject is much more complicated than can be summed up in a handful of sentences.<br /> <br /> It certainly isn't a new issue. For as long as I've been in this hobby (and to date myself, that's since the 90s) we've been discussing game balance. I've seen arguments about how D&amp;D2nd wizards are balanced against fighters because even though wizards completely dominate the late game, they pay for it by being useless in the early game. I bring that up not because it is laughable (though it is a bad game design philosophy, in my opinion) but as an example of how old this discussion is.<br /> <br /> As a shared endeavor, RPGs hinge on everyone involved trying to keep things balanced, the players, the game master, the writers, everyone. It's not about keeping people from feeling challenged, and it is not about making sure everyone is numerically equal. It is about a much more complicated kind of balance, that of engagement, expectations, effect on the story, and a whole host of other things. Where that centerpoint is will change from group to group and game to game, but it is the lifeblood of the gaming table.<br /> <br /> Experienced players and game masters know how to handle that balance, it's a large part of what makes them experienced. Hell, experienced groups can make a great game of a bad system because they know what they will have fun with, and how to communicate when they aren't having fun. Not everyone who plays a game is going to be experienced enough to navigate around the pitfalls, though, which means that every pitfall has the potential to make new players leave the game. So if you can deal with the pitfalls in the development stage... But this is a bigger discussion than this thread needs, several decades bigger in fact.<br /> <br /> None of which is to say that nerfing the upper levels of the Arcanoi was the best way to handle balance. But discussing how and why it works or doesn't work is a much more productive topic of conversation than ascribing motivations. The former at least leads to better understanding of the mechanics and possible alternatives. The latter...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T17:40:11-07:00","id":1253431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1253188#post1253188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess in an age where the new generation needs to have their participation ribbons, that mentality has bled its way into the rpg world. Tone down the more powerful characteristics of the game mechanics in order to make everyone seem ... Equal ... even though this is supposed to be a Horror related game, where Equality is a luxury; because that means you haven't met the big bad bump in the night ... yet!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am happy to inform you, with some degree of authority on this particular matter, that you have no idea what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> - C.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T21:02:36-07:00","id":1255998,"title":"","content":"His reasons may be false, or arguable... but the facts that are causing him concern are undeniable.<br /> <br /> The level 5 powers are in many cases, completely under-powered. I highlighted this in a previous post and inmy opinion, there is no rational reason behind this - it is rather arbitrary (example look at Keening and Moliate vs Usury and Pandemonium or Outrage). It is unfortunate that a product that did many things correctly, pretty much hobbled itself when it comes to what it makes it a game rather than a novel - the rules.<br /> <br /> To answer the OP, we are not finding it much of anything. We only purchased the one PDF, and shelved it, with no interest in purchasing any upcoming products from the line (if any are even forthcoming).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","user":"Nerhesi","date":". 09-21-2018, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T17:34:19-07:00","id":1256290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1250528#post1250528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess in an age where the new generation needs to have their participation ribbons, that mentality has bled its way into the rpg world. Tone down the more powerful characteristics of the game mechanics in order to make everyone seem ... Equal ... even though this is supposed to be a Horror related game, where Equality is a luxury; because that means you haven't met the big bad bump in the night ... yet!<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>hahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T17:37:55-07:00","id":1256291,"title":"","content":"I really like it. I don't care that the higher level arts were nerfed a little. I'm keeping my shelf of old wraith books for the extra lore and the options, but Wraith20 is the only book I'll be bringing to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T17:45:10-07:00","id":1256293,"title":"","content":"Currently, Wraith has been mainly used as a reading book for myself. We had planned to possibly use it this year, but that plan was overrun by the slightly later than expected delivery, which gave V5 a headway into the groups enthusiasm towards playing a WoD campaign.<br /> <br /> What I like about Wraith: 20th is:<br /> <br /> - It really does look gorgeous.<br /> - There really is some poetic writing included throughout the setting chapters.<br /> - It provides a 'completion' to the WoD20 line of games, which may be important if you've been collecting them, but also lends a whole world view of how each game makes up the WoD. There doesn't appear to be anything mechanically missing - like the absense of a Willpower entree in the trait list (like previous editions).<br /> - It includes spinoffs like Orpheus and The Risen.<br /> - Despite being a large, inclusive book, it seems to keep a tight focus on it's original themes well. It's very obvious how the game aspires to be played and gives good tools to support this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T02:04:45-07:00","id":1256402,"title":"","content":"I love Wraith 20 a lot. I've been using 2e powers, but I did that for a lot of Changeling too (same problem with massive power overhaul). But, in general, everything else in Wraith 20 is better. The powers are just one thing, and in those places where the levels are the same, the Wraith 20 write-up is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T02:10:44-07:00","id":1256667,"title":"","content":"Initially I though that Wr20 was trash, I really dislike some of the elements that are 'canon' such as every wraith having to be released from their caul and the whole crappy soul-forging economy idea that some people seem overly keen on.<br /> <br /> So while I wouldn't want to participate in a straight up 'standard' Wraith campaign (although possibly some of the alternative campaign suggestion would be cool) there is a ton of useful stuff in the book that adds a whole new dimension (literally!) to any form of crossover game and that alone makes the book more than worth the purchase price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T02:15:33-07:00","id":1256669,"title":"","content":"With a certain amount of bias, I can say this edition is the best one my group have played. All the players have remarked that this, to them, is the definitive Wraith game and we've all been having great fun in our chronicle. It's always gratifying to see players enjoying a game you worked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 09-24-2018, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T10:49:18-07:00","id":1256749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1256667#post1256667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Initially I though that Wr20 was trash, I really dislike some of the elements that are 'canon' such as every wraith having to be released from their caul</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a section on removing your own Caul... I'm confused.<br /> <br /> &quot;System: In order to remove her own Caul, a wraith must come to terms with the knowledge that she has died, and then<br /> spend 1 Willpower. The wraith then rolls Willpower, difficulty 4, with each success adding 1 Pathos to her normal starting total. (280)&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm also genuinely curious why you don't like the soulforged economy. I don't recall it being that different from what's in the Artificer's book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 09-23-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T11:21:07-07:00","id":1256763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1256749#post1256749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a section on removing your own Caul... I'm confused.<br /> <br /> I'm also genuinely curious why you don't like the soulforged economy. I don't recall it being that different from what's in the Artificer's book.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all - I've only read Wr20 rulebook and the 'Guide for the Recently Deceased' intro book, no previous versions, no supplements, etc.<br /> <br /> Secondly it's an ethos thing, I don't like that the characters have to start as victims with little agency until someone comes along and 'fixes' them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Caul cushions the shock of arrival on a new plane of existence; however, it\u2019s almost impossible to break out of on your own </div> </div> </div>Wr20 Handbook for the Recently Deceased p7<br /> <br /> Thirdly, and this is another ethos point - I don't like that people are treated as commodities - that just mirrors our modern world far too much and it's a weaksauce piece of lore based on a <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Film/SoylentGreen\" target=\"_blank\">no longer shocking common meme</a> that has been explored much better in other media.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T20:45:19-07:00","id":1256875,"title":"","content":"It's fine that you don't like the lack of agency, but I just quoted you a system from the book that gives any character a way out of their caul. Your whole troupe could use it. It costs I WP (temporary) and has a difficulty of 4, which is really easy, akin to a +2 or +3 in nWoD. The fluff may say it's &quot;nearly impossible&quot; to remove one oneself, but the system lets players do it rather easily.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's a simple fix to just let people out of their cauls on their own efforts most of the time and have most Legion recruiting be voluntary.<br /> <br /> As for the souls-as-commodities thing, I have much to say about it, but I suspect it's just not your bag.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T20:53:05-07:00","id":1256878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1256763#post1256763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secondly it's an ethos thing, I don't like that the characters have to start as victims with little agency until someone comes along and 'fixes' them:<br /> <br /> Thirdly, and this is another ethos point - I don't like that people are treated as commodities - that just mirrors our modern world far too much and it's a weaksauce piece of lore based on a <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Film/SoylentGreen\" target=\"_blank\">no longer shocking common meme</a> that has been explored much better in other media.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...if that's the case, why do you even bother with Wraith to begin with?<br /> <br /> If I was in your shoes, this would be headlong in &quot;no buy&quot; territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T03:53:33-07:00","id":1256925,"title":"","content":"As I said before, there's no way I'd be interested in participating in a 'default ' wealth game, the canon lore is just too repellent. As a sourcebook for a crossover game however it's an excellent resource","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T23:04:35-07:00","id":1257313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1256925#post1256925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, there's no way I'd be interested in participating in a 'default ' wealth game, the canon lore is just too repellent. As a sourcebook for a crossover game however it's an excellent resource</div> </div> </div> </div>...this coming from the guy who, in a different post, is ok with making a wraith &quot;henchman&quot; to a Giovanni?<br /> <br /> What, it's fine for the vampires to enslave the ghosts but not for the ghosts to do it to each other? And how the Giovanni have historically never been very nice to the ghosts they interact with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 09-26-2018, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T07:08:54-07:00","id":1257357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1257313#post1257313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...this coming from the guy who, in a different post, is ok with making a wraith &quot;henchman&quot; to a Giovanni?<br /> <br /> What, it's fine for the vampires to enslave the ghosts but not for the ghosts to do it to each other? And how the Giovanni have historically never been very nice to the ghosts they interact with?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a significant difference between playing a game you don't like and using those same rules to flesh out (pun intended) an NPC using all the options.<br /> <br /> Please take your strawman and burn it somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T10:40:11-07:00","id":1257399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1257357#post1257357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a significant difference between playing a game you don't like and using those same rules to flesh out (pun intended) an NPC using all the options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pray tell how is an NPC different from playing a PC? You're still engaging in a theme you considered problematic, and I fail to see how this doesn't apply. Especially in the way how you viewed the setting elements in absolutes with no compromises after others offered a route around it.<br /> <br /> Or that many vampires known for treating living and undead people as commodities...and that the Jyhad war can be boiled down to elders using neonates and ancilla as pawns and things in their games and not people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 09-26-2018, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T02:50:37-07:00","id":1257539,"title":"","content":"Why are you trying to start an argument? I don't have to justify anything to you, random stranger.on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T08:48:07-07:00","id":1257578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1257539#post1257539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you trying to start an argument?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said I was trying to start an argument?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't have to justify anything to you, </div> </div> </div>And besides, you brought up something in a public forum. So that leaves it open for anyone to discuss it. If you really didn't want anyone to talk back on it, why did you bring it up in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> random stranger.on the internet. </div> </div> </div>Also that's great, belittling my responses as &quot;random stranger on the internet&quot; instead of actually trying to address my points. Truly, a mature way of going about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T11:52:03-07:00","id":1263637,"title":"","content":"why where the basics removed and not replaced, many of those arts aren't replicated. with the power of many of the higher level costing too much or just Nerfed, if you look at V:tm or W:ta, Mage they got lots of new gifts,Routes or what have you and wraith we got a few new art and i mean a few, plus the many alt arts that are in other books just got left by the wayside and the non-Stygian arts got nothing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T20:29:01-08:00","id":1266853,"title":"","content":"I was, and am, a Wraith fan from at least back in the 2nd edition days. Wraith 20 is a fine book... that could have been better.<br /> <br /> Mage 20 provide many sets of boxed text where <i>variation</i>s of the metaplot were discussed. For example, maybe the Technocracy is riddled with Nephandi, maybe it is not. Maybe the Avatar storm still rages, and maybe it does not. M20 discusses the possibilities of the setting after the end of the previously published material.<br /> <br /> Wraith 20 does not explore this, except to detail Orphus. Wraith 20 is too proscriptive in this sense, meaning it is too limiting when compared to M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T01:36:32-08:00","id":1267223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1266853#post1266853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith 20 does not explore this, except to detail Orphus. Wraith 20 is too proscriptive in this sense, meaning it is too limiting when compared to M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. It's a little bit hard to do with Wraith since the meat and potatoes would boil down to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Did the spirit nuke happen?<br /> <br /> Yes- Then stop playing, the Underworld is gone.<br /> <br /> No- The Underworld is still around, go about your business&quot;<br /> <br /> ...also you might as well say all of the other WoD20 gamelines are too limiting since none of them did anything to the equivalent of Future Fates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T04:33:38-08:00","id":1267254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1267223#post1267223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean. It's a little bit hard to do with Wraith since the meat and potatoes would boil down to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Did the spirit nuke happen?<br /> <br /> Yes- Then stop playing, the Underworld is gone.<br /> <br /> No- The Underworld is still around, go about your business&quot;<br /> <br /> ...also you might as well say all of the other WoD20 gamelines are too limiting since none of them did anything to the equivalent of Future Fates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. As I recall, Ends of Empire ends with the group being crowned (masked?) the new Deathlords and the ones to shepherd the remaining Wraiths through the 6GM. So there was plenty of indication that some form of Dark Kingdom of Iron would exist. In addition there was even a thriving fan community for a while that wrote supplements for a post 6GM world. They focused on now isolated Necropoli weathering the aftereffects of the Maelstrom. Adding to that the (once canon) Orpheus storyline and every possibility between its barren Underworld and the one we see in Wr20 and you have a lot of possibilities to mix and match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T20:43:07-08:00","id":1267498,"title":"","content":"This is my point. M20 presents a lot of information and flexibility. W20, by comparison, does not. Ramnesis is correct; Ends of the Empire concludes with a lot of possibilities for what came next. Orpheus did not - it was a pared to the bone post-apocalyptic situation in terms of the Shadowlands. W20 presents situation as on the eve of the final disasters, but no other options. For W20 it is an either/or situation. M20 presents a number of sliding scales. W20 is not bad, it is just not are nuanced and interesting as M20. It I keep harping on that is it because it seemed the people behind M20 saw what V20 looked like, and what Werrewolf20 looked like, and decided to do one better. The people involved in W20 did not do that.<br /> <br /> My own take on a post 6th Maelstrom is something like Europe following the collapse of the Western Roman Empire. The Eastern Roman Empire still exists, but if you are not sheltered in it, you will face a lot of turmoil. If you are in it, you probably face a semi-stable tyranny. I do not know what city fulfills to role of Byzantium in this scenario - the heir to Rome or Stygia in this case. It might be Chicago, to tie it in closely with the forthcoming book .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T23:04:51-08:00","id":1267780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1267498#post1267498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ends of the Empire concludes with a lot of possibilities for what came next.</div> </div> </div> </div>...so did ALL of the End Times books.<br /> <br /> They all provided multiple choice on how each gameline could end (Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension, Time of Judgement) with all varying degrees of either following or not following it.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, it was Brucato's choice to do the Future Fates stuff in M20, not an OPP directive. It's nice to have, but it's not really something that makes or breaks Wraith20 or Changeling20 and choosing to do their own thing. With Wr20 making the choice of just having it set before the 6GM, and C20 making the choice of continuing/resolving the metaplot by having High King David being found and brought back. Which alright. That's the dev's choice.<br /> <br /> And that's without taking into account the hellish development Wr20 went through.<br /> <br /> (although from what I understand, out of the Big 5, Changeling is the least-metaplot depended so it not having its own Future Fates is very inconsequential and nobody cared)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:52:13-08:00","id":1267825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1267780#post1267780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's nice to have, but it's not really something that makes or breaks Wraith20 or Changeling20 and choosing to do their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was bad, just that M20 is better by comparison - a more flexible tool for gamers than the proscriptive Wr20.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T14:02:50-08:00","id":1269346,"title":"","content":"Its fine, could be better. I wish they had not changed the Arcanoi so much. I am ending up having to just use a buncha 2nd Edition stuff, in particular giving Fatalism some more Oracular flair back and Sandmen the ability to do their Theater since they removed Elysia for some reason and replaced it with Sleepy Sense. (Has it been explained why Sandmen lost their ability to do their signature Theater thing?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T17:29:03-08:00","id":1270990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1266853#post1266853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was, and am, a Wraith fan from at least back in the 2nd edition days. Wraith 20 is a fine book... that could have been better.<br /> <br /> Mage 20 provide many sets of boxed text where <i>variation</i>s of the metaplot were discussed. For example, maybe the Technocracy is riddled with Nephandi, maybe it is not. Maybe the Avatar storm still rages, and maybe it does not. M20 discusses the possibilities of the setting after the end of the previously published material.<br /> <br /> Wraith 20 does not explore this, except to detail Orphus. Wraith 20 is too proscriptive in this sense, meaning it is too limiting when compared to M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different strokes for different folks I guess but I found Future Fates to be the most pointless part of the M20. It boiled down to :<br /> <br /> 1 - use the whole metaplot event as presented<br /> 2- use only the parts of the event that you want<br /> 3 - don't use the event or change its outcome<br /> <br /> And repeat that umpteen of times. I don't need to be reminded thouand times that it's my game and I can run it however I see fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":". 11-26-2018, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T22:28:12-08:00","id":1271046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248244-how-are-you-liking-wr20?p=1267825#post1267825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said it was bad, just that M20 is better by comparison - a more flexible tool for gamers than the proscriptive Wr20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really?<br /> <br /> Like, I don't NEED the metaplot to run an interesting chronicle. I got enough ideas to pick from: personal tale of reaching Transcendence, slice-of-(un)life in Stygia, Renegades trying to bring down the corrupt system of the Hierarchy, combat heavy Doomslaying in the Labyrinth, Guild work and trying to stay a step ahead of any Hierarchy shenanigans, trying to make it as a Ferryman, exploring the other Dark Kingdoms, doing the Risen jig, or an alt-chronicle as being a Spectre.<br /> <br /> All stuff that's not metaplot-dependent and are flexible enough to take whatever form they can. Seems fine to me.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> Even then, it's kind of unfair to compare it to Mage.<br /> <br /> Since even before M20, Mage was known for being so flexible that you could do pretty much any genre in fiction within a Mage chronicle and it would always make sense. It's the type of flexibility that none of the other WoD gamelines were built for, because Mage was always about what your Will is being your Reality.<br /> <br /> Wraith was not designed for that intention. Neither was Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 11-27-2018, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T09:46:08-08:00","id":1271474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't need to be reminded thousand times that it's my game and I can run it however I see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the storyteller that needs to be reminded, it's the players! Way too many people who play this game insist on all the canon being exactly as presented in the books, it's one of the drawbacks of having too much fluff in WW books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}